'''Sifr Coop.''' (from [[Bayani]] صِفْر; {{lit|zero|cypher}}; and stylized as ''ṣifr'') is a Baliscan [[W:Artificial intelligence|artificial intelligence research]] and [[W:Information technology|information technology]] [[w:worker's cooperative|cooperative]] that develops [[W:Large language models|large language models]] (LLMs). It was founded in May 2023, after being [[w:Business incubator|incubated]] by the [[Confederal Internet Cooperative]]. Sifr is strictly a software and intelligence company, and thus it does not manufacture hardware; instead, it optimizes its code to run efficiently on the processors produced by the [[Essential industry|state-owned]] [[Baliscan Semiconductor Corporation]] (BSC).

Unlike Western tech giants that operate proprietary "black box" models, Sifr has adopted a "radical openness" philosophy, releasing the weights and source code of its powerful large language models (LLMs) to the public. The company actively recruits AI researchers from top Baliscan universities and also hires from outside traditional [[W:Computer science|computer science]] fields to broaden its models' knowledge and capabilities.

